1) do the hosekeeping: analyse docs, especially PROJECT_PLAN and features - derive the desired state, analyse the code - derive the current state, if there's a gap - generate a TODO.md in the project's root or  under .claude/ or other dedicated dir
2) review the docs in the project's root and propose a scema to organize them
3) add to the TODO or a dedicated (feature) doc a decription for the following feature: "smart github repo fetcher"; the idea is to avoid brute force: read `readme`, *.md (and other doc) files in the root of a repo and under doc/, docs/ or similar folders, look at the topic list - and decide whether to dig further, and only if the answer is "yes"  - then clone and analyze the whole repo. The specific algorithm could differ, but the point is gradual, adaptive repo analysis
